Rejected honestly: no generator is shipped.

The paper’s Theorem 1.5 proves an extremal \(O(k\log k)\) wheel-minor packing/transversal bound, not hardness for a generated distribution. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1710.06282v3)

The retained Track-B candidate passed every local gate, but failed hardening decisively:

- Bare oracle: 14/15 verified solves.
- Sizes tested: 193, 277, 401, 809, and 1621 vertices.
- Reference scan at shipping seed: 40,527 adjacency probes.
- Compact symmetry route: 204 exact operations.
- Exact answer density: \(1/1{,}264{,}040{,}099{,}700\).

The models consistently recognized the supplied order-four symmetry, so enlarging the graph did not create no-tool difficulty. Track A was also unsupported by the paper or distributional evidence.

